#: wraithguard/gui/conflicts.py:1338
msgid "The same scan with the load order's own shape restored: plugin, then kind of record, then record, with the record compared across every plugin that defines it.\n\nA flat list answers 'what conflicts'. This answers 'what does this mod change, and where does it lose', which is the question you are actually asking. Run 'Plugin summary' first to colour it in. Read-only."
msgstr ""

#: wraithguard/gui/conflicts.py:1349
msgid "Plugin summary..."
msgstr ""

#: wraithguard/gui/conflicts.py:1354
msgid "Judge every conflict in the list and count the result per mod, rather than per record.\n\nA flat list of conflicts cannot answer the question that decides load order: which of my mods is losing work? This compares each record field by field and counts, for every plugin, how many records it edits and does not get its way on.\n\nReads every conflicting record with tes3conv, so it takes a moment on a large load order. Read-only."
msgstr ""

